{
  "id": "p4",
  "title": "if, then, else",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "p4-l1",
      "title": "if … then",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "if condition then statement runs the statement only when the condition is true. Conditions compare values with = <> < > <= >= (<> means \"not equal\").",
        "Remember: = compares and := stores. In a condition you always use =.",
        "The result of a comparison is a boolean, so you can also store it: hot := temp > 30;"
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Weather;",
          "var",
          "  temp: integer;",
          "begin",
          "  write('Temperature? ');",
          "  readln(temp);",
          "  if temp > 30 then",
          "    writeln('Hot! Stay in the shade.');",
          "  if temp < 0 then",
          "    writeln('Freezing!');",
          "  writeln('Have a nice day.');",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "Temperature? 34",
          "Hot! Stay in the shade.",
          "Have a nice day."
        ],
        "inputs": [
          "34"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p4-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does <> mean in Pascal?",
          "options": [
            "Not equal",
            "Less or greater, but not both",
            "Swap the values",
            "Smaller than"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "a <> b is true when a and b are different."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Size;",
            "var",
            "  n: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  n := 12;",
            "  if n > 10 then",
            "    writeln('big');",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "big",
            "small",
            "nothing",
            "an error"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "n is 12, and 12 > 10 is true."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-l1-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Print zero when n is 0.",
          "code": [
            "  if n ___ 0 then",
            "    writeln('zero');"
          ],
          "options": [
            "=",
            ":=",
            "==",
            "<>"
          ],
          "answer": "=",
          "explanation": "A single = compares in Pascal."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-l1-e4",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program doesn't compile. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "program Check;",
            "var",
            "  x: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  x := 5;",
            "  if x := 5 then",
            "    writeln('five');",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 5,
          "explanation": ":= stores, but a condition needs = to compare: if x = 5 then."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-l1-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Skip;",
            "begin",
            "  if 3 > 7 then",
            "    writeln('yes');",
            "  writeln('done');",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "done",
            "yes\ndone",
            "yes",
            "nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "3 > 7 is false, so only the last writeln runs."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-l1-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What type does a comparison like a < b give?",
          "options": [
            "boolean",
            "integer",
            "char",
            "real"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "true or false."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4-l2",
      "title": "else and begin … end",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "else gives the other way: if a > b then writeln(a) else writeln(b); There must be no semicolon before else: the ; would end the if, and Turbo Pascal stops with Error 113.",
        "To run several statements after then or else, group them with begin … end. Without it, only the first statement belongs to the if.",
        "Chains with else if pick one of several cases."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Grade;",
          "var",
          "  points: integer;",
          "begin",
          "  write('Points? ');",
          "  readln(points);",
          "  if points >= 90 then",
          "    writeln('Grade A')",
          "  else if points >= 75 then",
          "    writeln('Grade B')",
          "  else if points >= 50 then",
          "    writeln('Grade C')",
          "  else",
          "  begin",
          "    writeln('Grade F');",
          "    writeln('Try again next time.');",
          "  end;",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "Points? 82",
          "Grade B"
        ],
        "inputs": [
          "82"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p4-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why is there no semicolon before else?",
          "options": [
            "The ; would end the if statement, and else would be left alone",
            "Semicolons are never allowed in an if",
            "It's just a style choice",
            "else needs a colon instead"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Error 113: Error in statement."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-l2-e2",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program doesn't compile. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "program Sign;",
            "var",
            "  n: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  n := -4;",
            "  if n >= 0 then",
            "    writeln('positive');",
            "  else",
            "    writeln('negative');",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 6,
          "explanation": "The ; after writeln('positive') ends the if, so else has nothing to belong to."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-l2-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Pick;",
            "var",
            "  x: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  x := 8;",
            "  if x < 5 then",
            "    writeln('A')",
            "  else",
            "    writeln('B');",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "B",
            "A\nB",
            "A",
            "nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "x < 5 is false, so the else part runs."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-l2-e4",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Group the two statements so both run only when ok is true.",
          "code": [
            "  if ok then",
            "  ___",
            "    writeln('Saving…');",
            "    writeln('Saved.');",
            "  end;"
          ],
          "options": [
            "begin",
            "do",
            "then",
            "{"
          ],
          "answer": "begin",
          "explanation": "begin … end makes several statements count as one."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-l2-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Trap;",
            "var",
            "  n: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  n := 0;",
            "  if n > 0 then",
            "    writeln('first')",
            "  else",
            "    writeln('second');",
            "  writeln('third');",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "second\nthird",
            "first\nthird",
            "third",
            "second"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "n > 0 is false, so the else part prints second. The last writeln isn't part of the if, so it always runs."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-l2-e6",
          "type": "order_lines",
          "prompt": "Put the lines in order: print even or odd.",
          "lines": [
            "if n mod 2 = 0 then",
            "  writeln('even')",
            "else",
            "  writeln('odd');"
          ],
          "answer": [
            "if n mod 2 = 0 then",
            "  writeln('even')",
            "else",
            "  writeln('odd');"
          ],
          "explanation": "if … then, the statement without ;, else, the other statement."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4-l3",
      "title": "and, or, not",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "and, or and not combine conditions. In Pascal, and and or are stronger than comparisons, so each comparison needs brackets: if (age >= 13) and (age <= 19) then …",
        "Without brackets, Turbo Pascal reads age >= 13 and age <= 19 as age >= (13 and age) <= 19, and stops with an error.",
        "not flips true and false: if not found then …"
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Teen;",
          "var",
          "  age: integer;",
          "  member: boolean;",
          "begin",
          "  age := 15;",
          "  member := false;",
          "  if (age >= 13) and (age <= 19) then",
          "    writeln('Teenager');",
          "  if (age < 6) or (age >= 65) then",
          "    writeln('Free entry')",
          "  else if not member then",
          "    writeln('Ticket: 9.00');",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "Teenager",
          "Ticket: 9.00"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p4-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why do comparisons need brackets with and/or?",
          "options": [
            "and and or are stronger than <, > and =",
            "Brackets make it faster",
            "It's only a style rule",
            "They don't"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Without brackets, and grabs the numbers next to it first."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-l3-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is (5 > 3) and (2 > 4)?",
          "options": [
            "FALSE",
            "TRUE",
            "5",
            "an error"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "and needs both sides to be true; 2 > 4 is false."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-l3-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is (5 > 3) or (2 > 4)?",
          "options": [
            "TRUE",
            "FALSE",
            "2",
            "an error"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "or needs just one true side."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-l3-e4",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Print OK when x is between 1 and 10.",
          "code": [
            "  if (x >= 1) ___ (x <= 10) then",
            "    writeln('OK');"
          ],
          "options": [
            "and",
            "or",
            "not",
            "&&"
          ],
          "answer": "and",
          "explanation": "Both must be true: and."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-l3-e5",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program doesn't compile. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "program Range;",
            "var",
            "  n: integer;",
            "begin",
            "  n := 7;",
            "  if n > 0 and n < 10 then",
            "    writeln('one digit');",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 5,
          "explanation": "Each comparison needs brackets: if (n > 0) and (n < 10) then."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-l3-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "program Door;",
            "var",
            "  open: boolean;",
            "begin",
            "  open := false;",
            "  if not open then",
            "    writeln('closed')",
            "  else",
            "    writeln('open');",
            "end."
          ],
          "options": [
            "closed",
            "open",
            "TRUE",
            "nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "not open is true, because open is false."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
